  "references": [
    {
      "id": "k-sunflower-background-67",
      "topic": "background",
      "summary": "Annual oilseed with a deep root system where soil permits. Cold sensitivity varies by stage; seedling responses do not establish flowering tolerance. Heat and drought near flowering and seed filling can reduce seed set and oil yield. Sclerotinia has a broad host range; a different broadleaf crop may still maintain it. Water uptake can extend deep into the soil; rooting depth is constrained by compaction, available profile depth and moisture.",
